From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:30:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/etnaviv: Take all resets of the core

The driver gets the first reset of the node only. A core that has more
than one reset line stays partly in reset, and its registers read as
zero.

Use the reset control array helper, which asserts and deasserts all
resets of the node together, as panfrost does. A node with one reset or
none is handled as before.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; the driver releases
all four resets of the NPU and the core identifies itself, where it read
as model 0 with the first reset only.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_gpu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_gpu.c
index 5c23182f4d33..c4375859dfe9 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/etnaviv/etnaviv_gpu.c
@@ -1922,7 +1922,7 @@ static int etnaviv_gpu_platform_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 
 	/* Get Reset: */
-	gpu->rst = devm_reset_control_get_optional_exclusive(&pdev->dev, NULL);
+	gpu->rst = devm_reset_control_array_get_optional_exclusive(&pdev->dev);
 	if (IS_ERR(gpu->rst))
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(gpu->rst),
 				     "failed to get reset\n");
